  "body": "Chrome used to follow the focus fixup rule one, but the behavior was counter-intuitive\nand other browsers (Firefox/Safari) do not follow the rule.\n\nMake the fixup rule one better aligned to what Firefox/Safari do; when focused area is\nremoved, instead of moving the focus to the first focusable area in the control group,\nremember the old focused position as a \"focus navigation starting point\" to be used\nlater for TAB focus navigation.\n\nAddresses #704 \n",
